home/{print $1" "$2}'` only outputs the id and title, but the `list` output is `id
 title`, and title is "alpha note #home #zeta" — that is, the title contains a space
. Therefore $2 only gets the first word of the title ("alpha"), dropping the rest
. The filtered output `home` is the full line, so the comparison is failing due to
 a script bug, not an app bug.

